From 63886b97066831eeba44e648d5b54c43aa92799a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 09:09:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 222/226] add openssh-sftp package: bundle sftp-server for SFTP
 over dropbear

Stage 2 (SFTP binary): dropbear ships the SFTP subsystem enabled but no
sftp-server binary. Vendor OpenSSH 9.8p1 as the openssh-sftp package and build
ONLY its sftp-server target, cross-compiled against the in-tree openssl 1.1.1w
+ zlib, installed to /usr/libexec/sftp-server (matches dropbear/localoptions.h
SFTPSERVER_PATH). Nothing else from OpenSSH is built or shipped - dropbear
remains the SSH server; no sshd/ssh/scp/ssh-keygen from this tree.

router/Makefile:
- obj-$(RTCONFIG_SSH) += openssh-sftp (built alongside dropbear)
- openssh-sftp/stamp-h1: cross-configure (--host, --without-pam/selinux,
  --without-openssl-header-check, CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS -> in-tree openssl+zlib)
- openssh-sftp / -install (install+strip) / -clean rules

Verified: make rt-be96u (as reaper) MAKE_EXIT=0; sftp-server is an ARM EABI5
binary at fs/usr/libexec/sftp-server; image builds. SFTP now works once the
user enables SSH (Administration > System); it inherits the sshd_enable gate
and runs as the SSH user.
